include "../../../linux.mereo"

-- `leave words when "hello".size < 8` reads `5 < 8` -- a CONSTANT expression,
-- the same on every path, which is what a spliced template leaves behind when
-- its length argument is a literal. The scope is left every time and the body
-- never runs, so `[small + "hello".size - 8 : 1]` -- an offset of -3 -- cannot
-- happen and is not something to ask a bound for.
--
-- Constant expressions ONLY, deliberately. Asking the analysis for a name's
-- value instead read it at one point and called it the value everywhere:
-- `leave parse when plen == 0` inside a loop answered 0 from the entry path
-- and marked 149 live steps unreachable in loglyze, whose accesses were then
-- never classified at all.
program goes
  small is 4 bytes
  d is 0
  terminal is already linux.file (descriptor is 1)
  words goes
    leave words when "hello".size < 8
    d is [small + "hello".size - 8 : 1]
  end
  [small : 1] is d
  terminal.write (buffer is small, count is 1)
end
